joe_doufu schrieb:
> 
> I have: gray dragon scale mail, amulet of reflection, dexterity gloves,
> speed boots, invisibility and magic resist cloaks (+ dwarf, elf,
> leather), helm of brilliance +0 (i think), and a hawaiian shirt +5.  I
> think I ought to get: gauntlets of power, ESP helm, rings of conflict,
> levitation, protection, a cockatrice corpse, and perhaps a cloak of
> protection?  Perhaps a new pet or two as well.

Knights can cast spells quite well (but they have trouble learning
them); for that, enchanting your helm of brilliance and getting a robe
would be perfect. A cloak of protection has no merit over a robe apart
from one point of base AC; a helm of ESP will not give you anything
new - you already have always-on ESP from your quest artefact. Rings
of protection aren't worth a wish.

A cockatrice corpse is only ever worth a wish when you have something
incredibly evil breathing down your neck _right now_. It's a corpse
and will rot away after a while.

> Does polypiling ever produce good, magical equipment like the above? 

'ever' - yes. 'reliably' - no.
To unpack: junk gear (ordinary armour pieces like the stuff dropped by
soldiers) will typically polymorph into other junk gear. The chance of
non-magical armour to 'morph into magical stuff is so small that the
entire Ludios scrap heap will turn into another non-magical scrap heap
with perhaps two or three magical pieces strewn in. 

To have a good chance at getting magical armour, you need to polymorph
magical armour pieces. Fortunately, this includes fumble gloves/boots
and (i think) elven boots and cloaks. 

I find polymorph most beneficient when used on surplus rings, scrolls,
potions, wands and (magical) tools.

> Final question: should a knight add a ranged weapon?  If so, what works?

Magic missile works great. Seriously, if you get your hands on some
low-level spellbooks, read them. Knights can advance in attack spells
and get a nice damage bonus on spells when carrying the magic mirror.

Other than that, you _can_ use a bow, but you can do just as well
without. 

